# SparkTower — mobile (Expo)
#
# Copy to `mobile/.env`. Expo inlines every `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` variable into the
# app bundle, where anyone who unpacks the binary can read it. So:
#
#   NEVER put a secret here — no SESSION_SECRET, MOBILE_TOKEN_SECRET, API key,
#   client *secret* or token. Secrets live only on the server (the root .env).
#
# What belongs here are the OAuth *client ids* Google issues per platform. They
# are public by design; the server verifies Google's id token against the same
# ids (GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID / GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID in the root .env).
#
# No defaults: blank means unset, and the app then turns Google sign-in off on
# that platform rather than borrowing another id. A release build needs its
# own real ids.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=

# The API base URL. app.json's `expo.extra.apiUrl` now defaults to the
# production host (https://sparktower.app) so that no build can ship pointing
# at a laptop; set this to point a local run at a local server instead.
#
# A localhost value is rewritten for you per platform: 10.0.2.2 on the Android
# emulator, your LAN address on a physical device over `expo start`. Leave it
# unset to talk to production from a development build.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:5001
